// Creates a ThemeShadow. The shadow of the theme (WinUI
// `Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Media.ThemeShadow`): set as the `Shadow` of an element, the element casts
// the shadow of its elevation, the Z of its `Translation`, as the controls of WinUI do under
// their popups (32 for a flyout, 16 for a tool tip, 128 for a content dialog). WinUI 3 draws
// every theme shadow as a drop shadow ([`is_drop_shadow_mode`](Self::is_drop_shadow_mode)): an
// ambient and a directional shadow around the element, the darker in the dark theme, none in a
// high contrast theme. A `ThemeShadow` can be shared by several elements; it has no appearance
// of its own. [`receivers`](Self::receivers) are the elements the projected shadows of WinUI
// (the root and the open popups by default) would fall on. WinUI 3 keeps the collection and
// its validation but does not draw projected shadows, so the receivers do not change the
// drawing here either.
fn themeShadow() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 440)
