// Creates a TitleBar. The title bar of a window (WinUI's `TitleBar`): a back button, a pane
// toggle button, a left header, an icon, a title and a subtitle, content (a search box, in
// WinUI Gallery) and a right header, drawn in the title bar of the window when the client area
// extends into it. The control sets the states of WinUI as pseudo-classes, which the control
// theme of the WinUI theme (`src/FerroUI.Themes.WinUI/Controls/TitleBar.xaml`) styles:
// `:back-button-visible`, `:pane-toggle-button-visible`, `:left-header-visible`,
// `:icon-visible`, `:title-text-visible`, `:subtitle-text-visible`, `:content-visible`,
// `:right-header-visible` (the Visible states of their groups; their absence is Collapsed),
// `:deactivated` (the Deactivated states: the window is not active), `:expanded-height`
// (HeightGroup: content or a header), `:compact` (DisplayModeGroup: the content no longer fits
// beside the title) and `:negative-inset-spacing` (LeftHeaderSpacingGroup). The template parts
// are WinUI's: `LeftPaddingColumn` and `RightPaddingColumn` (borders in FerroUI, a column
// definition has no name), `PART_BackButton`, `PART_PaneToggleButton`, `PART_Icon`,
// `PART_LeftHeaderPresenter`, `PART_ContentPresenterGrid`, `PART_ContentPresenter` and
// `PART_RightHeaderPresenter`. The Fluent and Simple themes have no template for it
// (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, section 5.1). The window: WinUI's `AppWindow` gives the
// insets of the caption buttons, the drag regions and the activation. The port takes the
// insets from [`Window::caption_button_insets`] (the traffic lights of macOS at the left, the
// caption buttons the toolkit draws at the right), marks the title bar as the drag region of
// the window and its back button, pane toggle button, headers and the interactive controls of
// its content as elements that take the input ([`WindowDecorationProperties`] roles, which
// take effect while the client area extends into the decorations), and follows
// [`WindowBase::is_active`]. A title is the title of the window while the bar shows it, as in
// WinUI.
fn titleBar() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 452)
