fn visualLayerManager() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 492)
// Creates a VisualState. A visual state: the values its [`setters`](Self::setters) set while
// it is the current state of its [`VisualStateGroup`](super::VisualStateGroup). The
// [`storyboard`](Self::storyboard) of the state runs while it is the current state; the
// storyboard of the state it leaves stops (its values are removed). The setters are setters
// with a [`target`](ferroui_base::styling::Setter::target): markup writes `<Setter
// Target="Element.Property" Value="..."/>`. They are applied at animation priority, above
// local values and styles, and removed when the group leaves the state
// (docs/porting/winui-calculator-gaps.md, section 5.5). Deviation
// (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, VisualStateManager): `x:Name` names the state but does not
// register it in the name scope, so `find_name` does not find it.
fn visualState() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 493)
// Creates a VisualStateGroup. A group of mutually exclusive [`VisualState`]s: at most one of
// them is the [`current_state`](Self::current_state) of the group, null at first. The groups
// of an element are the attached
// [`VisualStateManager::visual_state_groups_property`](super::VisualStateManager::visual_state_groups_property);
// `VisualStateManager::go_to_state` changes the state of the group that has the state of the
// name it is given.
fn visualStateGroup() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 494)
// Creates a VisualStateManager. Manages the visual states of controls and the transitions
// between them. The visual states of an element are the
// [`visual_state_groups_property`](Self::visual_state_groups_property) attached to the root of
// its visual states: for a templated control the root of its template, for a user control (or
// any content control, or content page) whose template has none, the control that is its
// content. [`go_to_state`](Self::go_to_state) makes a state the current state of its group. A
// custom manager derives from this class, overrides
// [`go_to_state_core`](VisualStateManagerImpl::go_to_state_core) and is set on the root with
// [`set_custom_visual_state_manager`](Self::set_custom_visual_state_manager).
fn visualStateManager() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 495)
// Creates a VisualTransition. How a [`VisualStateGroup`](super::VisualStateGroup) changes from
// one state to another when `GoToState` is called with transitions (WinUI's
// `VisualTransition`). A transition applies from the state named [`from`](Self::from) (empty:
// any) to the state named [`to`](Self::to) (empty: any). It runs its
// [`storyboard`](Self::storyboard) and, over [`generated_duration`](Self::generated_duration)
// eased by [`generated_easing_function`](Self::generated_easing_function), animations it
// generates from the values of the old state to those of the new one; the setters and the
// storyboard of the new state apply when they have completed.
fn visualTransition() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 496)
// Creates a Window. A top-level window.
fn window() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 497)
// Creates a WindowDrawnDecorations. Manages client-side window decorations (app-drawn window
// frame). This is a logical element that holds the decorations template and properties. The
// host of the top-level extracts the overlay, underlay and popover visuals from the template
// content and inserts them into its own visual tree. Pseudo-classes: `:normal`, `:maximized`,
// `:fullscreen`, `:has-shadow`, `:has-border`, `:has-titlebar`, `:has-maximize`,
// `:has-fullscreen`, `:has-minimize`, `:has-close`, `:has-title`.
fn windowDrawnDecorations() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 501)
// Creates a WindowDrawnDecorationsContent. Holds the template content for
// [`WindowDrawnDecorations`](super::WindowDrawnDecorations). Contains three visual slots:
// underlay, overlay, and fullscreen popover.
fn windowDrawnDecorationsContent() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 502)
// Creates a WindowNotificationManager. An [`INotificationManager`] that displays notifications
// in a window.
fn windowNotificationManager() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 503)
// Creates a WrapPanel. Positions child elements in sequential position from left to right,
// breaking content to the next line at the edge of the containing box. Subsequent ordering
// happens sequentially from top to bottom or from right to left, depending on the value of the
// `Orientation` property.
fn wrapPanel() -> int = ferro_create(typeId: 504)
// Creates a XamlAmbientLight. The ambient light of Reveal (WinUI's internal
